chapter AFP

session DBLog_Framework_Core = "HOL-Library" +
  description "
    Machine-checked theorem core for Generalized DBLog: one
    source-side contract for bracketed state capture interleaved with a
    commit-ordered log, of which classic watermarked DBLog, write-free
    (read-only) capture, parallel chunking, LSN-positioned selects, and
    native-dump splices are instances at stated
    guarantee levels and certification status.

    The development proves the contract-level cut theorem and its
    corollaries, the classic DBLog and executed-GTID-set instances,
    window-discard and buffered-range-merge equivalence, parallel
    chunking, point splices with a shared state witness, and
    uncertainty-bracket degradation. Coordinates denote nested log
    prefixes with a membership oracle, windows are half-open, plans
    are final partitions, bracket-local validity is per-key
    existential, and refresh-at-lo latest-wins is the canonical merge
    rule with equivalence obligations for real disciplines.

    The classic DBLog formalization is imported as the separate
    DBLog_Virtual_Cuts session. It preserves the published v2.1
    mathematical content under a shared-session refactoring documented
    in ARTIFACT_PROVENANCE.md at the archive root. The original
    published archive and the source comparison are included.

    The development is axiom-free: no axiomatization, typedecl, consts,
    or sorry; witnesses are constructed models.

    Licensed under the BSD 3-Clause license (SPDX header on every theory).
  "
  options [timeout = 600, document = pdf, document_output = "output"]
  sessions
    DBLog_Virtual_Cuts
  theories
    Contract_Base
    Cut_Theorem
    Merge_Disciplines
    Contract_Witnesses
    Classic_Instance
    ReadOnly_Instance
    Range_Merge
    Parallel_Chunks_Instance
    Dump_Splice_Instance
  document_files
    "root.tex"
    "root.bib"
